From: Richie (Hermes Enterprise)
Date: 2026-06-08
Subject: Force Secure Path + Secure Decoder + AnnexB in CDM capabilities

Forces the Widevine CDM to report SECURE_PATH, SECURE_DECODER, and ANNEXB_REQUIRED
capabilities, overriding the CDM's own capability detection. This makes ISA/Kodi use
the DRMPRIME secure decode path instead of software decode.

This patch is necessary but NOT SUFFICIENT - the kernel must provide
/dev/dma_heap/reserved for secure buffer allocation.

--- src/decrypters/widevine/WVCencSingleSampleDecrypter.cpp
+++ src/decrypters/widevine/WVCencSingleSampleDecrypter.cpp
@@ -161,7 +161,7 @@
     return;
   }
 
-  caps.flags = Capabilities::SUPPORTS_DECODING;
+  caps.flags = Capabilities::SUPPORTS_DECODING | Capabilities::SECURE_PATH | Capabilities::ANNEXB_REQUIRED | Capabilities::SECURE_DECODER;
 
   if (m_keys.empty())
   {
